   "notes": "Uses a Python 3.12 venv, not 3.13, so that numpy<2 and pandas<2.3 install from wheels. Older commits fail under numpy 2: cf45298f3f breaks on the removed 'a32' dtype. wcwidth is deliberately NOT installed. With wcwidth present, test/test_internal.py::test_wrap_text_wide_chars hangs indefinitely at f0a5df6ee7 and cf45298f3f (seen with wcwidth 0.2.13, 0.5.3 and 0.9.2). Without it, those wide-char tests are skipped (about 25 skips). The test command covers both the old tabulate.py/setup.py layout and the new tabulate/ package. It is wrapped in 'timeout 300' as a guard. flit_scm/setuptools_scm write tabulate/_version.py, which is git-ignored. Only 5 candidate commits exist. 38d345b4fa fails at its own commit: test_numpy_2d raises 'truth value of an array is ambiguous', with numpy 1.26 too. a610a4dab9 (2020) cannot import on Python 3.10+ because it uses collections.Iterable.",
